[COUNT label=history] data.loyaltyPointsHistory.items[*?amount=@td(MSN_ORDERCOUNT.reward)].length = {{REWARD_COUNT_BEFORE}} + 1 {SPEC} — exactly one new Earned entry at this mission's reward amount. NOT pinned to the order: a mission-granted ledger entry carries object = null (measured live 2026-08-28 on the VIP fixture — all four known mission rewards 750/450/550/400 have a null object, while every product-earn entry carries type CustomerOrder + orderNumber), so .object.orderId cannot be asserted for a mission grant. Amount + count delta is the maximum the API permits; the missing attribution is BL-LOY-015.
[DATA label=history] data.loyaltyPointsHistory.items[?amount=@td(MSN_ORDERCOUNT.reward)].amount = @td(MSN_ORDERCOUNT.reward) {SPEC}
[DATA label=history] data.loyaltyPointsHistory.items[?amount=@td(MSN_ORDERCOUNT.reward)].object is null {OBSERVED} — recorded, not endorsed: a mission grant carries NO object, so it is attributable to neither a mission nor an order. Asserting the measured shape makes a future build that starts populating object fail this line loudly, at which point the case is upgraded to pin the order. It is the BL-LOY-015 violation made visible, not a behaviour anyone wants.

