[COUNT label=history_after] data.loyaltyPointsHistory.items[*?amount=0].length = {{ZERO_AMOUNT_COUNT_BEFORE}} {SPEC} — narrowed 2026-08-28 from a whole-history total (which co-completing missions with NONZERO rewards can move without ZEROREWARD granting anything) to a count of amount=0 entries specifically. SCHEMA LIMITATION (confirmed via live introspection): the schema has no mission-identifying field on a history item, and the filter grammar cannot compound object.orderId with amount in one expression, so this is the closest available proxy for 'no entry attributable to this mission's zero-reward completion' — not a true per-order-and-mission attribution. A currentBalance=BAL_BEFORE equality was also dropped outright (not weakened to a relation): co-completing missions can add an UNBOUNDED, unpredictable amount to the balance on this env, so no valid relation on currentBalance exists for a zero-reward case at all.

