[DATA label=order_status_after_setup] body.status = Cancelled {DOC} — positive control (prove-then-assert, same pattern as MSN-029's isStarted guard): confirms the out-of-band status change actually landed BEFORE the unchanged-state assertions below are trusted. [SETUP] is parsed but never executed by graphql-runner.ts (recognized only as a step-tag boundary — knowledge/api/graphql-test-cases-runner.md §3); without this guard the case would silently pass the reversal assertions below against an order that was NEVER cancelled. Under the automated runner alone this line FAILS (nothing executes the cancellation) — this case only exercises the reversal question when the out-of-band script from Preconditions is run by hand immediately before dispatch.
